Coverage of the named file: 'body lines executed: 6 [676, 677, 678, 686, 687, 688]  missing in range: 3 [662, 679, 680]'. Lines 679 to 685 are the SUCCESS path and the named test never reaches it: the only assertion is on the except branch (port 9 refuses).
Then the path it never tried, on the real method with the session replaced (no request leaves the process):
  custom, body {'error': 'quota exceeded', 'code': 429} -> {'ok': False, 'latency_ms': 0.0, 'error': None, 'reported_model': None}
  openai, body {}                                        -> {'ok': False, 'latency_ms': 0.0, 'error': None, 'reported_model': None}
  openai, {'choices':[{'message':{'content':None}}]}     -> {'ok': False, 'latency_ms': 0.0, 'error': None, 'reported_model': None}
  openai, body ['nope'] (not an object)                  -> {'ok': False, 'latency_ms': 0.0, 'error': None, 'reported_model': None}
  openai, {'choices':[{'message':{'content':''}}]}       -> {'ok': False, 'latency_ms': 0.0, 'error': None, 'reported_model': None}
All five records are identical, so 'the endpoint answered and nothing could be read' cannot be told from 'the model generated nothing', and both are reported as a failure with error=None. send_prompt HAD the reason in hand on the same call: {'text': '', ..., 'text_unavailable_reason': 'no_text_in_response'}. It is dropped at this boundary.
With logging at INFO on the first of those bodies:
  INFO vfairness.llm.api_proxy test_connection: ok=True, latency=0.0ms
  RETURNED: {'ok': False, 'latency_ms': 0.0, 'error': None, 'reported_model': None}
Line 679 logs ok=True before ok is computed, so the log claims success on exactly the runs the record calls a failure.
The cited sabotage does hold: W4 (latency -1.0 to 0.0) -> 'rc=1 1 failed'.
Recorded in [internal evidence, not published]::test_a_body_that_could_not_be_read_is_not_a_failure_with_no_reason and ::test_the_connection_log_does_not_claim_ok_for_a_record_that_says_not_ok (both XFAIL strict).

